# Server only. Never expose these to the client bundle.
AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=southeastasia

PRONUNCIATION_PROVIDER=azure
MAX_AUDIO_SECONDS=15
MIN_AUDIO_SECONDS=0.25

# NOT READ BY THE SERVER. The SNR gate (T10) runs client-side before upload,
# and its threshold is the `minSnrDb` default in src/speech/capture/recorder.ts
# and src/speech/react/useRecorder.ts. Kept here because PRD §9 lists it and
# TASKS T10 names it, but changing this value has no effect today — change the
# recorder default, or wire this through to the client, instead.
MIN_SNR_DB=10

MONGO_URL=mongodb://localhost:27017
MONGO_DB=sonare

# Required to use the #/diagnostics screen's read endpoints — unset means
# they're disabled (fail closed), not open. Set it, then visit
# #/diagnostics?token=<value> once; it's remembered after.
DIAGNOSTICS_TOKEN=

# Optional. Total scoring calls allowed per UTC day, across all callers — a
# ceiling independent of the per-IP rate limit, since every scored attempt is
# a billed Azure API call.
MAX_DAILY_SCORING_CALLS=2000

# Optional. How long attempts/diagnostics records survive in MongoDB before
# a TTL index removes them automatically.
RETENTION_DAYS=90

# Diagnostic only. When set, the exact WAV sent to the scorer is written
# here. Off by default — audio is normally never persisted. Unset it when the
# debugging session is over; never set it where real learners are served.
# SAVE_AUDIO_DIR=./audio-debug

# Optional. Provider price per audio-hour for your region and tier, used only
# to turn the #/diagnostics usage figures into money. Deliberately unset by
# default: a wrong rate displayed as cost is worse than no cost at all,
# because nobody re-checks a number that looks authoritative. With this unset,
# diagnostics reports exact call counts and audio duration and omits money.
# Verified 2026-09-02 for speech-to-text Standard in southeastasia: 1.00 USD
# per audio hour. Pronunciation assessment is not a separate meter. Raise to
# 1.30 if enableProsodyAssessment is ever switched on (a 0.30/hr add-on).
# AZURE_SPEECH_RATE_PER_AUDIO_HOUR=1.00
# AZURE_SPEECH_RATE_CURRENCY=USD

# Signs anonymous learner tokens (server/identity.ts). No default and no
# fallback: unset means learner identity and sync are disabled, the same rule
# DIAGNOSTICS_TOKEN follows. A built-in default would put the signing key in
# the repository and let anyone forge any learner.
# Generate one with: node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
LEARNER_TOKEN_SECRET=

# Optional. How long a device-link code can be claimed for, in seconds
# (server/linkCodes.ts). Default 600 — ten minutes. Minutes rather than hours
# on purpose: the code is a bearer credential that grants full read, write and
# delete access to one learner's record, and its expiry is half of the
# brute-force arithmetic written out in linkCodes.ts. Raising it weakens that
# arithmetic; lengthen the code instead. Clamped to 30..3600, and an
# unreadable value falls back to the default with a warning.
# LINK_CODE_TTL_SECONDS=600

# ── the model voice (ElevenLabs) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Synthesises the phrase a learner imitates, generated once per content
# version and cached (scripts/generate-model-voice.ts). Unset means the whole
# feature is simply absent: every language falls back to the browser's own
# synthesiser, which is what shipped before this existed. Nothing breaks.
#
# Only our reference text is ever sent. No learner audio goes to this provider
# and no code path accepts any — that would make it a second processor of
# learner voice recordings, which is not a decision to take by accident.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# The model. `eleven_v3` is the default and the only one declaring all five
# languages this product needs: multilingual_v2, flash_v2_5 and turbo_v2_5
# cover fr/es/de/hi but none of them declares Kannada. An unknown name falls
# back loudly rather than being sent, because a model with no declared
# language list cannot be guarded — and a model asked for a language it does
# not speak answers 200 with a mispronunciation, not an error.
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_v3

# The voice per language, as `locale:voiceId` pairs. Overrides the table in
# server/services/elevenLabs.ts without a code edit. A voice is the accent a
# learner will imitate, which is the variable this product measures, so a
# language with no voice chosen is refused rather than spoken in the
# placeholder's English accent.
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_IDS=fr-FR:xxxx,hi-IN:yyyy
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=oneVoiceForEveryLanguage

# Where generated audio is cached. Relative to the working directory, and
# git-ignored — it is reproducible build output, not source. A fresh deploy
# has none until the script has run, so every language falls back until then.
# MODEL_VOICE_CACHE_DIR=voice-cache

# Ceiling on synthesis characters per UTC day, counted separately from the
# scoring cap. Deliberately a second budget: a day of generating audio must
# not be able to consume the allowance for scoring learner attempts.
# MAX_DAILY_VOICE_CHARACTERS=50000

# ── alert thresholds (server/infra/alerts.ts, surfaced on GET /metrics) ──────
# Evaluated when /metrics is read; there is no daemon. Point a scraper at it
# with the diagnostics token and alert on `.alerts.firing` — an unscraped
# server evaluates nothing, so this is half a system until something reads it.
#
# A rate that is null stays `unknown`, never `ok` and never firing: null means
# "not enough data", and treating it as zero is the exact falsehood the metrics
# layer was built to avoid.
#
# 0.15 is ~2x the measured indeterminate rate (7.2% across 139 real attempts)
# and ~3.5 standard errors above it at that sample size. Set at the baseline it
# would fire on noise about half the time.
# ALERT_INDETERMINATE_RATE=0.15
# Half the 8s at which a single attempt is abandoned.
# ALERT_PROVIDER_P95_MS=4000
# Fraction of the daily scoring cap at which to warn.
# ALERT_SPEND_CAP_FRACTION=0.8
# Below this many scoring calls both statistical rules stay `unknown`. Without
# it, one indeterminate result out of one is a 100% rate and would fire on the
# first bad take after every deploy.
# ALERT_MIN_SCORING_CALLS=50
